        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Barsha",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Mall of the Emirates opened in 2005, featuring Dubai's first indoor ski slope, and sparked rapid residential growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Barsha",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Al Barsha sits in western Dubai, bordered by Al Sufouh, Emirates Hills, Jumeirah Village Circle, Dubai Motor City, Al Quoz, and Dubai Hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Barsha",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "RTA buses and the Mashreq Metro station connect Al Barsha to the Mall of the Emirates, while feeder buses link the station to interior residential zones.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7,
        8,
        9,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Barsha",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Al Barsha is home to the Dubai Community Theater and Arts Centre and the History of Cinema Museum, showcasing visual media from shadow play to modern film.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Barsha",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "South of Al Barsha lies the Dubai Miracle Garden, one of the world's largest flower gardens, adjacent to the climate‑controlled Dubai Butterfly Garden.",
